halo 2 is one of the most competitive  games in the franchise the player base  broke the boundaries of multiplayer  which skyrocketed the skill ceiling with  glitches that define the title's meta  and are still used by pros to this day  later in halo 2 if you didn't know these  glitches you couldn't compete especially  in ffa for sure because it's all about  speed and timing and then also in fours  if you  dropped a bxr in a clutch situation that  might be four dead for your team and you  lost the game they really molded  halo 2 into kind of a hybrid between a  fighting game and a shooter because  you had to know these very precise  inputs to really keep up with the speed  of the game that's eli the ninja who's a  legendary halo player who made waves in  halo 2 and 3 in the mlg circuit he even  has a call out on midship named after  him and in my opinion he's absolutely  correct despite my fighting game  background i was technically doing my  first tournament combos in halo 2 which  was a little while before i ever played  my first actual fighting game street  fighter 4. funnily enough just as the  earliest street fighter combos were  actually unintentional glitches halo 2's  famous bxr bxb and others came about in  a very similar fashion today we're  checking out those game-changing  glitches as we take a little stroll down  memory lane leave a like subscribe and  let's get into it  we're starting with my favorite the bxr  is where you may like to break an enemy  shields and then glitch the gun to shoot  immediately afterward the names of the  glitches are pretty much how you perform  them so b for beatdown then x and then r  in a quick succession to create the  sense to kill combo the glitch occurs  when you try to reload your gun but  there is nothing to actually reload  whether that be a full clip or your  final one that means you can't do it if  your clip is half full however the game  still reads the reload input which can  then be cancelled into a gunshot despite  the bxr being used mostly with a battle  rifle you can still use this combo with  any weapon in the game a carbine bxr  just hits a little bit different  if you weren't bxr you just were not  going to be at the top i mean  every single pro player could be xr and  vxb  and if you weren't doing those things  your team was not going to succeed  either mastering this technique is not  as daunting as it may sound but can  actually be performed in an alternative  way that is still just as effective if  you swap the x and the r and input brx  you can still get the same desired  effect and instant kills the bxr turned  anyone into a power weapon of their own  and made you feel as if you were  carrying around a shotgun at times i  remember playing online  and walking past the guy  and i just died instantly and i was so  confused i was like what just happened  to me you know i thought he was cheating  at first i said how is it possible that  he just killed me instantly  and it took me a while to figure it out  and then later come to find out he had  bxr'd me and that was like my first  introduction to the bxr was getting  destroyed by this guy who did it  repeatedly another use for the bxr was  the free extra shots you get before the  clip reloads itself the game still reads  the x input and your gun will reload in  about the same time it would have taken  if you perform the animation that's why  you'll often see people starting their  br battles with the bxr no matter the  distance  however most reload glitches won't work  if you have hosts which is basically  when the game chooses you as the server  for the game custom matches usually give  host to the party leader and luckily mcc  has dedicated servers for matchmaking  i mentioned earlier that you'll often  see players use bxr to start their br  fights for extra shots but another  useful reason why it's used is because  you can cancel the tail end of the  reload animation with a beat down for  faster recovery combo that beat down  into an xr and you're now in motion  knowing you can cancel the reload  animation with a beatdown is obviously  going to lead us to the bxb  in the early unpatched version of halo 2  this combo is basically useless because  it took way too many beatdowns to kill  anyone however eventually beatdowns were  fixed and turn into a two hit kill  this turned the bxb into a close range  powerhouse especially if bxr wasn't at  your disposal but unlike the bxr you  could perform the bxb no matter what  your current clip situation is looking  like full half or empty and you could do  it pretty much infinitely if you needed  to  halo 2 classic in mcc can be a little  annoying at times because the beatdowns  don't always register like how they used  to but i suppose we could just chalk  that one up to port problems  excuse me  my melee that's  the double shot and the quad shot is one  of the most difficult techniques in the  game that still have practical value if  you have the execution in my opinion the  good old double shot is where players  really began to stand out from the rest  and showed what it really meant to be  the best at the game and luckily for us  this is one of eli's favorite glitches  because he's one of the best to ever do  it the double shot is a beautiful glitch  so you press rr and x with a battle  rifle normally you just shoot  battle rifle repeatedly so it'd be like  if we're going to use onomatopoeia here  but if you could figure out the double  shot you could essentially shoot a  six bullet burst  instantly so just like  it's just like a double  double shot literally but it was very  high risk and high reward because if you  mess up you're either stuck reloading or  you're stuck in this animation where you  can't really do anything this is  remedied by carrying a secondary weapon  to quickly swap with timing your yy  weapon swap correctly results in a  nearly instant swap back and forth to  your primary weapon which cancels that  reload jam and allows you to perform rrx  again for a quad shot alright it's such  a beautiful glitch and it's it's not  overpowered because if you mess up  you're you're screwed you're gonna die  the grenade reload glitch is definitely  the easiest and most practical glitch in  the game and there's really no drawback  to using it whenever you throw an aid  tap xx in a quick succession during the  throwing animation and voila that's it  if you don't have hosts your gun will  simply reload itself a few seconds later  combining this with the bxr reload and  you can unleash a nearly non-stop  barrage of bullets and catch your  opponents off guard when their clip runs  short  it's such an easy tactic to implement  into your game plan that you'll catch  yourself doing it every time you throw a  name so keep an eye out in case you do  have hosts so you can adjust your  gameplay accordingly and just for  clarity you can't do the glitch if you  don't have any needs  i remember when i learned all these  little combos back in the day and i  can't even picture what halo 2 was like  without them  they become synonymous with my rose  tinted nostalgia for halo 2 multiplayer  the countless hours i spent online and  at lans and became the foundation of how  i looked at competitive gaming  and knowing this skill ceiling existed  heightened my respect for the pros and  made me even more passionate about the  game but to put a pause on all of the  nostalgia for just a moment it's  important to remember that halo infinite  is the beginning of a completely new era  of halo esports eli himself is going to  be the head coach for our g1 officials  very first halo team and will be a part  of defining a meta for a completely new  chapter and it's really awesome to know  that glitches are kind of how eli got  his start in all of this to be honest  with you before i was a competitive  gamer all i was interested in was  glitches and games i mean as a little  kid growing up i was always on those  like websites like  the cheat codes for goldeneye on  nintendo 64 or like little tricks to get  outside the map  so i would say probably the first glitch  i learned in halo  was uh from like reading the online  forums and learning like the super  bounce like the super bounce is  something that  people can't even experience anymore  because they took it out of the current  versions of the game  with that said i want to know what your  favorite glitches so leave a comment  down below and if you enjoyed this video  please leave us a like we'll be covering  even more cool halo things here on  gamespot so subscribe before you go so  you don't miss out thanks so much for  watching and we'll see you next time  peace  [Music]  you

